## 7 · BELIEF SEQUENCE — BS-AV1 (backward chain, presented forward)

**Backward derivation (destination first):**
- `final_buying_belief` = FB-AV1 + BB-V: "A store that gets several small, capped tries is how I finally get a steady income of my own — and I'd rather give it that second try now than let the first store be the last word." (Q-O-0109, Q-Y-0027; BB-V lever from WHAT-MADE-THEM-ACT: Q-B-0004 "I was afraid to ever try again, but eventually I did", Q-Y-0015 "i failed the challenge … that's why i'm going to continue")
- ← just before: **B-104** (BB-I, live wire honored) "I'm right to guard my money — this time I can see every cost, the store and payouts are mine, no test spends a dollar I didn't approve."
- ← before that: **B-103** (BB-III, live wire honored) "It isn't easy money — and a store in my name that tests small first is a different setup from the one I was sold."
- ← before that: **solution requirement accepted** (BB-III) "the second try needs several small tries, read early."
- ← before that: **B-102 broken** (BB-II, THE ONE BELIEF) "my stores failing doesn't show I can't do this; each got one guess."
- ← before that: **B-107** (bridge, M-1) "a store finds what sells by testing several products small and early."
- ← before that: **B-105** "fixing the store and buying clicks for the same product didn't change it."
- ← before that: **B-101** "the product I tried didn't sell — and it was the only real try."
- ← **OPENING: B-106** "plenty of us lose on a first store" — held (Q-Y-0027), live_wire NO → stop.

**Forward (5 plain paragraphs — the page and ad read this as order, not copy):**
1. There's plenty of us who put money into a first store and lost it — you're not the only one who watched the clicks come in and the orders never did. And no, it isn't easy money, whatever the videos said. (B-106, B-103 agreed)
2. Your product didn't sell. That part is true. What nobody pointed out is that it was the only real try your store got — one product, or one batch switched on at once, and ads until the money ran out. Fixing the store and buying more clicks for that same product was never going to change the answer. (B-101, B-105)
3. The sellers who do end up with a product that sells mostly didn't get it on the first try. The ones who write about it tested five, sometimes ten products, each on a small budget, and cut what didn't move. Some had nine failed stores before the one that paid for the rest. (B-107, P-104, P-106)
4. So your store didn't prove this can't work for you. It proved one guess missed. What a second try needs isn't a better guess — it's several small tries, each on a budget you approve and can stop, with someone reading the results early and swapping what isn't selling, in a store that stays in your name. (B-102 broken → solution requirement)
5. That's how a Readymerce store is launched — in stages, not all at once — and you see every cost before you pay: the $500 build, then the platform fees and the ad budget you set. No income is promised, and the refund terms are written out with their conditions. If you still want the thing you started, it's worth giving it more than one shot. (B-104, BB-V; PT-04, PT-05, PT-09, PT-15, F-11)

| WHERE HE IS (Q-##) | WHERE HE MUST ARRIVE (B-##) |
|---|---|
| "the product did not sell, so I had to close the store" (Q-O-0108 [R-OWNED]) | B-101 → the product missed, and it was the only real try |
| "Ive had 2 stores on Shopify both failed" (Q-F-9004) · "I definitely was not an expert" (Q-Y-0039) | B-102 → the stores didn't show I can't do this; each got one guess |
| "I'm targeting different interests. Still no sales." (Q-F-0019) | B-105 → the next product, not more clicks for the same one |
| "make it seem like easy money when it's really not" (Q-Y-0016) | B-103 → not easy money, and a different, tested-small setup (live wire kept) |
| "I've been burned many times" (Q-Y-0030) · "Is that one-off payment or I need to make a regular payment?" (Q-O-0112 [R-OWNED]) | B-104 → every cost written first, store and payouts in my name, budgets I approve (live wire kept) |
| "i had to give up or else i would literally lose all my money" (Q-Y-0049) | final → a second try made of small, capped tries, started now |

- **opening_status:** FOUND — B-106 (Q-Y-0027, VALIDATED, live_wire NO)
- **belief_sequence[AV-01][]:** [B-106, B-101, B-105, B-107, B-102, SOLUTION-REQUIREMENT, B-103, B-104, FINAL(FB-AV1+BB-V)]

